  "notes": "A compound of {裁|さい} (cut, sew) and {断|だん} (cut off). Primarily used for cutting fabric to make garments, but also applies to cutting paper, especially in bookbinding where {裁断機|さいだんき} is a paper cutter/guillotine.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {裁断|さいだん}する — to cut (fabric/paper)\n- {裁断機|さいだんき} — paper cutter; cutting machine\n- {裁断|さいだん}{済|ず}み — pre-cut\n- {布|ぬの}を{裁断|さいだん}する — to cut fabric\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {細断|さいだん} — shredding (cutting into small pieces, as in a shredder)\n- {切断|せつだん} — cutting, severing (more general, including hard materials)\n- {裁縫|さいほう} — sewing, needlework (broader term that includes cutting and sewing)",
